+Custom renderer hosts can opt in to the native `caretGeometry` event on an
+`input` or `textarea` through the existing event-handler registry and native
+`setEventListener` mutation. It reports the same shaped insertion point and
+scroll offsets used by GPUI's caret: `x`/`y` are window coordinates, `width` is
+the native caret width, and `height` is the line height. Its JSON `value`
+contains `visible`, `fontSize`, `remainingWidth`, `offset`, `selectionStart`,
+and `selectionEnd` (UTF-8 byte offsets). Events are emitted only when geometry,
+selection, or focus changes, independently of blink opacity. Listening does
+not replace native input, IME, selection, or caret positioning.
+
